# CANONICAL fixture — kernel-hardening WP-B: an optional `regionAnchor` rebinds a
# profile whose stored V3 `regionId` was re-minted by a dimensional edit
# (SCHEMA §7.3 "Region anchor", §7.2 warning `REGION_REBOUND_BY_ANCHOR`).
#
# Recipe: a 40x20 rectangle with a circle centred ON its right edge at (40, 10),
# so the circle CROSSES the edge and the region table holds three bounded cells.
# A V3 id hashes the cell's bounding fragments including their intersection
# parameters, so changing the circle's radius re-mints every id in the sketch.
#
# Plan 1 (r = 6) extrudes the largest cell by its then-current id, with an anchor
# at (10, 10) — deep inside the rectangle, far from the circle. The exact id
# matches, so the anchor is never consulted and the step carries no warning.
#
# Plan 2 is the SAME plan with r = 7 and the SAME (now stale) id. The exact
# lookup matches nothing; the anchor still lies in exactly one cell, so that cell
# is bound, the step is `ok`, and `planStep` 1 carries the warning with
# `evidence.region.from/to/anchor`. `params` are never rewritten — the stored id
# stays stale and the rebind repeats deterministically on every regen, which is
# why plan 2 sends the same `regionId` bytes plan 1 did.
#
# The two ids are pinned literally (plan 3 re-sends the r=6 id WITHOUT an anchor, so
# a corrupted plan-1 id cannot be rescued by the anchor and hide). They are Rust-independent content hashes of
# the cell geometry, so a change to either value is a region-identity break and
# must be treated as one; `worker/tests/test_region_anchor.cpp` derives the same
# two ids from `buildRegionTable` and pins the volumes (800 - pi*r*r/2)*10.
#
# Plan 2 is a from-0 replay (D5: `expectedBaseHash` is the empty-prefix anchor),
# which is exactly the shape Rust sends for a parametric edit of step 0.
#
# The harness matches an array ELEMENT BY ELEMENT from index 0, so the pinned
# `diagnostics` order is load-bearing: the rebind warning must be the FIRST entry.
# This sketch has no degenerate entity, so no `SKETCH_ENTITY_DEGENERATE` warning
# precedes it today; anything that starts emitting one here must update this file
# rather than reorder the array, because the order IS part of the contract.
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"hello","seq":0}}
{"send":{"v":1,"t":"req","id":1,"verb":"OpenSession","args":{"documentId":"doc_region_anchor","documentRevision":0,"workerEpoch":4,"mode":"determinism"}}}
{"expect":{"v":1,"t":"resp","id":1,"ok":true,"result":{"sessionOpen":true}}}
# Plan 1 — r = 6. The id is fresh, so the anchor is not consulted.
